00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:30,160
What do we do about the outside influences in the lives of our Scouts?

119
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:35,520
To begin with, let's figure out what's outside and what's inside.

120
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:41,760
So for the purposes of this discussion, let's make this very, very simple. okay,

121
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:45,360
Outside influences on our Scouts are something that's beyond the scope of

122
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:49,120
our control as Scouts. Inside influences are

123
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:52,240
something within the scope of our control as Scouts.

124
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:55,920
So let's take a look at what's outside of our control.

125
00:06:55,920 --> 00:07:01,280
So pick any time in the last century or the century

126
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:04,560
preceding that, or indeed the one preceding that,

127
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:08,800
and you'll read about adults working with young people

128
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:12,640
battling the broader influences, the outside ones,

129
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:16,000
that they can't control, And confronting something you can't control

130
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,599
feels terrible, doesn't it? I mean, it's just very

131
00:07:19,599 --> 00:07:25,440
oh, it's upsetting and it takes up a lot of energy and a lot of time.

132
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:31,280
It's it's a kind of silly and it's also really aggravating and frustrating.

133
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:34,560
There's a lot of bad feeling that comes with it, isn't there?

134
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:39,440
You have a feeling of helplessness and you just try and

135
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:42,800
fight against things. I want to suggest a better way

136
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:46,000
of dealing with these things beyond our control. okay,

137
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:50,800
Because we're outnumbered, We're outgunned.

138
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:54,400
Here's how psychologist and social philosopher

139
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:59,440
BF Skinner put it in his book Walden II, He said each of us has interests

140
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:02,880
which conflict with the interests of everybody else.

141
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:07,760
Everybody else we call society. It's a powerful opponent and it almost

142
00:08:07,760 --> 00:08:11,120
always wins. Oh, here and there, an individual prevails

143
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:15,360
for a while and he gets what he wants. Sometimes he storms the culture of a

144
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:18,560
society and changes it to his own advantage,

145
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:25,920
But society wins in the long run, for it has the advantage of numbers and age.

146
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:29,120
So, while we're on this philosophical plane for a moment, we're all humans,

147
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:33,200
right, We're all swimming in a sea of influences, Call them what you may.

148
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:36,480
Some of them are within our control and some of them are outside of our

149
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:41,600
control, And these influences, for good or ill, have always been with us.

150
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:47,680
They're a part of what we'll call for the purposes of this discussion, the human

151
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:51,680
condition. Now, I hear from a lot of people and I

152
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:55,760
am. one of the common threads that I hear from scouts about

153
00:08:55,760 --> 00:09:00,960
is things like outside influences, like video games and cell phones, and the

154
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:05,600
level of involvement of the scouts, parents and things that are really not

155
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:09,920
within the scope of a scouter's control. Now, think about

156
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:13,040
this, okay, Because before we had cell phones and video

157
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:16,960
games to contend with, there was TV, and before TV there was radio. and before

158
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:20,880
radio there was moving pictures. and before moving pictures

159
00:09:20,880 --> 00:09:24,480
there was burlesque shows in vaudeville. and

160
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:28,640
before burlesque shows in vaudeville there were spicy novels.

161
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:32,720
and you know that guy Gutenberg, with his movable type, he caused a lot of

162
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:35,440
trouble. Now I'm not saying that influences that are

163
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:39,040
outside the scope of our control are are either

164
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:42,640
insignificant or they're totally objectively good

165
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:48,400
or bad. You know, we just have to accept the premise

166
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:52,640
that our scouts are subject to a number of influences beyond the scope of our

167
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:56,400
control. It's part of the human condition. So what do we do?

168
00:09:56,400 --> 00:10:00,560
Do we just give up or do we go to battle with these influences?

169
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:05,120
So let's get tie all of this to some very practical things we can apply in our

170
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:08,720
work as scouts. I think that if we go to battle with the

171
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:11,680
human condition, it means we're fighting a losing battle. Remember,

172
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:16,480
society wins in the long run, for it has the advantage of numbers and age.

173
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:20,400
Now you can look at something like that and you go, oh well, let's just give up.

174
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:23,760
then You know, we don't, we, there's nothing we can do.

175
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:27,600
so we'll just give up and let these influences roll over us and roll over

176
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:30,720
our scouts, and everything will go to hell in a hand basket.

177
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:34,480
But that's not what I'm saying. If battling the human condition is fighting

178
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:37,920
a losing battle, that doesn't mean that the only other option

179
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:42,320
is surrendering. I'm not saying that we're going to surrender,

180
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:45,840
but we have to get to a point to make some progress.

181
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:49,280
and when we accept that these influences have always been there and

182
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:52,960
they will always be there- they simply are what they are-

183
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:56,320
we're going to start making some progress. In his book

184
00:10:56,320 --> 00:11:00,480
Aids to Scout Mastership, Baden Powell discusses dealing with

