00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:13,280
hear applied to things like cell phones and the internet today.

188
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:17,120
But after he kind of examines the corrosive influence of moving pictures

189
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:20,640
on our youth, he encourages us to replace

190
00:11:20,640 --> 00:11:25,040
those influences with something positive. and he quoted me says:

191
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:30,319
you can't do this by forbidding or punishment, but by substituting

192
00:11:30,319 --> 00:11:35,839
something at least equally attractive but good in its effects.

193
00:11:35,839 --> 00:11:39,199
And over and over again in his writings Baden Powell talks about

194
00:11:39,199 --> 00:11:43,120
this very simple concept, and you know what it boils down to. it's kind of

195
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:45,920
trite and you've heard it a thousand times before.

196
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:49,839
it's better to light a single candle than to curse the darkness. so we don't

197
00:11:49,839 --> 00:11:53,520
give up. We don't let the broader influences of

198
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:56,640
the human condition just roll over us and say, well,

199
00:11:56,640 --> 00:12:01,199
nothing I can control, oh well, we'll just do it. but we don't go to battle with them

200
00:12:01,199 --> 00:12:04,079
either. What we do, we set up something that, as

201
00:12:04,079 --> 00:12:09,360
Baden Powell said, is equally attractive but good in its effects,

202
00:12:09,360 --> 00:12:13,520
And once I started doing just that, I learned

203
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:17,280
not to battle with these things anymore and I honestly I don't pay much attention

204
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:20,640
to them because it's really a waste of my time.

